# Tests for the Filing_status module

Run with `clerk test`. Each named scope is one concrete return, worked by hand
from IRC 1(c), 2(a), 2(b), 6013(a), 7703 and Pub. 501 (2024) pp 6-11 as quoted
in `catala/filing_status.catala_en`. Every scope sets satisfiable inputs (answers
a real filer could give), asserts the expected eligibility, and asserts that a
known-bad output is rejected (an ineligible chosen status is knocked out). The
oracle comparison is `make difftest SCOPE=filing_status` and
`make difftest-filing-status-graphs`.

> Using Types
> Using Filers as F
> Using Qualifying_child as Q
> Using Qualifying_relative as R
> Using Dependents_benefit_split as B
> Using Hoh_qss_persons as H
> Using Filing_status as S

## Helper: one return, with default answers

The default return: an unmarried filer (never married) born 1985-06-15, a US
citizen, not claimed by anyone, living in Florida, filing single, with no
household members. A second filer entry carries plain citizen answers (read
only when the marital status makes it the spouse). The optional household
member is the filer's biological son, born 2016-05-01 (8), unmarried, a US
citizen with an SSN, who lived with the filer all year, had no gross income,
did not provide over half of his own support, is nobody else's qualifying
child, and is claimed; the filer paid more than half the cost of keeping up
the home. A test overrides only what it tests.

```catala
declaration scope Case:
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context marital_status content F.MaritalStatus
  context year_of_spouse_death content F.YearOfSpouseDeath
  context secondary_is_citizen content boolean
  context secondary_is_resident content boolean
  context lived_together_all_year content boolean
  context lived_together_months content F.SpouseLivedTogetherMonths
  context can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death content boolean
  context has_child content boolean
  context child_residency content Q.ResidencyDuration
  context upkeep content boolean
  internal child content H.Member
  output r content S.FilingStatusReturn

scope Case:
  definition filing_status equals Single
  definition marital_status equals NeverMarried
  definition year_of_spouse_death equals DiedBeforeTaxYearMinusTwo
  definition secondary_is_citizen equals true
  definition secondary_is_resident equals false
  definition lived_together_all_year equals true
  definition lived_together_months equals LivedTogetherMoreThanSixMonths
  definition can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death equals false
  definition has_child equals false
  definition child_residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition upkeep equals true
  definition child equals H.Member {
    -- dependent: R.Member {
      -- person: Q.Person {
           -- relationship: Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
           -- date_of_birth: |2016-05-01|
           -- full_time_student: false
           -- permanent_total_disability: false
           -- residency_duration: child_residency
           -- own_support: false
           -- married: false
           -- writable_joint_return: false
           -- writable_required_to_file: false
           -- writable_filing_only_for_refund: false
           -- writable_could_be_qualifying_child_of_another: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_must_file: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_did_file: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund: false }
      -- answers: R.DependentAnswers {
           -- gross_income: $0
           -- writable_qr_support_test: true
           -- tin_type: R.TinType.Ssn
           -- is_us_citizen_full_year: true
           -- writable_us_resident: false
           -- writable_us_national: false
           -- writable_canada_mexico_resident: false
           -- tp_claims: true }
      -- split: B.BenefitSplitAnswers {
           -- has_other_biological_or_adoptive_parent: false
           -- non_parental_some_parent_not_claiming: false
           -- which_parent_not_claiming: B.WrittenDeclaration.NobodyDid
           -- in_parents_custody: false
           -- lived_with_tp_or_other_biological_or_adoptive_parent_more_than_six_months:
                false
           -- biological_or_adoptive_parents_living: false
           -- nights_with_tp_vs_other_parent: B.NightsComparison.Less
           -- tp_agi_higher_than_other_parent: false
           -- parents_meet_reqs_rule_for_children_of_divorced_parents: false
           -- special_rule_child_used_by_custodial_parent_as_qp: false
           -- special_rule_agi_test: false
           -- parental_situation: B.ParentalSituation.Other
           -- parental_support: false
           -- multiple_support_agreement: false } }
    -- upkeep: H.UpkeepAnswers {
         -- tp_paid_most_of_home_upkeep: upkeep
         -- tp_paid_most_of_parent_home_upkeep: false } }
  definition r equals
    output of S.FilingStatusReturn with {
      -- filing_status: filing_status
      -- marital_status: marital_status
      -- year_of_spouse_death: year_of_spouse_death
      -- primary_filer: F.FilerAnswers {
           -- date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
           -- is_blind: false
           -- can_be_claimed: false
           -- will_be_claimed: false
           -- potential_claimer_must_file: false
           -- potential_claimer_did_file: false
           -- is_us_citizen_full_year: true
           -- writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year: false
           -- writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year: false
           -- writable_is_national: false }
      -- secondary_filer: F.FilerAnswers {
           -- date_of_birth: |1986-02-20|
           -- is_blind: false
           -- can_be_claimed: false
           -- will_be_claimed: false
           -- potential_claimer_must_file: false
           -- potential_claimer_did_file: false
           -- is_us_citizen_full_year: secondary_is_citizen
           -- writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year: false
           -- writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year: secondary_is_resident
           -- writable_is_national: false }
      -- secondary_filer_date_of_death: |2022-03-01|
      -- primary_filer_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund: false
      -- mfj_required_to_file: true
      -- mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits: false
      -- lived_together_all_year_with_spouse: lived_together_all_year
      -- spouse_lived_together_months: lived_together_months
      -- writable_lived_apart_last_six_months: false
      -- writable_separation_agreement: false
      -- can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death: can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death
      -- in_registered_domestic_partnership: false
      -- filer_residence_and_income_state: FL
      -- spouse_itemizes: false
      -- mfs_living_spouse_filing_return: false
      -- mfs_deceased_spouse_filing_return: false
      -- mfs_spouse_has_gross_income: false
      -- members: if has_child then [child] else [] }
```

## The cases of issue #20

### Married, spouse a nonresident alien: no joint return

IRC 6013(a)(1): "no joint return shall be made if either the husband or wife
at any time during the taxable year is a nonresident alien". The spouse is
neither a citizen nor a resident (no 6013(g) election). The filer may file
separately; with no qualifying person, not as head of household. With the
son living with the filer, IRC 2(b)(2)(B) ("considered as not married ... if
at any time during the taxable year his spouse is a nonresident alien") makes
the filer a head of household (Pub. 501 p 9, Nonresident alien spouse).
Known-bad output rejected: choosing MFJ is knocked out.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMarriedNraSpouse:
  alone scope Case
  with_child scope Case
  chose_mfj scope Case

scope TestMarriedNraSpouse:
  definition alone.marital_status equals Married
  definition alone.secondary_is_citizen equals false
  definition alone.filing_status equals MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition with_child.marital_status equals Married
  definition with_child.secondary_is_citizen equals false
  definition with_child.filing_status equals HeadOfHousehold
  definition with_child.has_child equals true
  definition chose_mfj.marital_status equals Married
  definition chose_mfj.secondary_is_citizen equals false
  definition chose_mfj.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  assertion not alone.r.eligible_for_mfj
  assertion alone.r.eligible_for_mfs
  assertion not alone.r.eligible_for_single
  assertion not alone.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion not alone.r.eligible_for_qss
  assertion alone.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion not alone.r.unsupported
  assertion alone.r.recommended_filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately
  assertion not with_child.r.eligible_for_mfj
  assertion with_child.r.filer_could_qualify_for_hoh
  assertion with_child.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion with_child.r.eligible_for_mfs
  assertion with_child.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion not with_child.r.unsupported
  assertion with_child.r.recommended_filing_status = HeadOfHousehold
  # Known-bad: a joint return with a nonresident alien spouse
  assertion not chose_mfj.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion chose_mfj.r.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
  assertion chose_mfj.r.unsupported
```

### Married, lived apart the last six months, with a child: head of household

IRC 2(c) and 7703(b): a married filer who files separately, keeps up a home
for more than half the year for a child the filer can claim, and whose
spouse was not a member of the household during the last 6 months, "shall
not be considered as married" (Pub. 501 p 8, Considered Unmarried). The
spouses lived apart all year; the son lived with the filer all year. MFJ and
MFS stay eligible (Pub. 501 p 7). Known-bad outputs rejected: the same filer
living with the spouse all year is not a head of household, and choosing HoH
is then knocked out; the filer is married, so single is never eligible.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMarriedLivedApartWithChild:
  c scope Case
  together scope Case
  chose_single scope Case

scope TestMarriedLivedApartWithChild:
  definition c.marital_status equals Married
  definition c.lived_together_all_year equals false
  definition c.lived_together_months equals LivedApartAllYear
  definition c.has_child equals true
  definition c.filing_status equals HeadOfHousehold
  definition together.marital_status equals Married
  definition together.has_child equals true
  definition together.filing_status equals HeadOfHousehold
  definition chose_single.marital_status equals Married
  definition chose_single.lived_together_all_year equals false
  definition chose_single.lived_together_months equals LivedApartAllYear
  definition chose_single.has_child equals true
  definition chose_single.filing_status equals Single
  assertion c.r.eligible_for_mfj
  assertion c.r.eligible_for_mfs
  assertion c.r.filer_could_qualify_for_hoh
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_people_count = 1
  assertion c.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_single
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_qss
  assertion c.r.has_multiple_eligible_filing_statuses
  assertion c.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion not c.r.unsupported
  assertion c.r.treat_as_hoh
  # DF: chose HoH, so not "wants a separate return": the recommendation is MFJ
  assertion c.r.recommended_filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
  # Known-bad: living together, no HoH
  assertion not together.r.filer_could_qualify_for_hoh
  assertion not together.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion not together.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion together.r.unsupported
  # Known-bad: a married filer cannot file single
  assertion not chose_single.r.eligible_for_single
  assertion chose_single.r.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
```

### Widowed in 2023 with a dependent child: qualifying surviving spouse, not head of household

IRC 2(a)(1): the spouse "died during either of his two taxable years
immediately preceding the taxable year", the filer keeps up a home that is
the principal place of abode of a son whom the filer can claim, and a joint
return could have been made for 2023 (2(a)(2)(B)). IRC 2(b)(1): a head of
household "is not a surviving spouse". Known-bad outputs rejected: choosing
HoH is knocked out; choosing single is knocked out too (IRC 1(c) excludes
surviving spouses, DF-BUG(20-a)); without the joint-return answer the filer is
not a surviving spouse and becomes a head of household.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestWidowedYearMinusOneWithChild:
  c scope Case
  chose_hoh scope Case
  chose_single scope Case
  no_joint scope Case

scope TestWidowedYearMinusOneWithChild:
  definition c.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition c.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedTaxYearMinusOne
  definition c.can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death equals true
  definition c.has_child equals true
  definition c.filing_status equals QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
  definition chose_hoh.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition chose_hoh.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedTaxYearMinusOne
  definition chose_hoh.can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death equals true
  definition chose_hoh.has_child equals true
  definition chose_hoh.filing_status equals HeadOfHousehold
  definition chose_single.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition chose_single.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedTaxYearMinusOne
  definition chose_single.can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death equals true
  definition chose_single.has_child equals true
  definition chose_single.filing_status equals Single
  definition no_joint.marital_status equals Widowed
  definition no_joint.year_of_spouse_death equals DiedTaxYearMinusOne
  definition no_joint.has_child equals true
  definition no_joint.filing_status equals HeadOfHousehold
  assertion c.r.filer_could_qualify_for_qss
  assertion c.r.qss_qualifying_people_count = 1
  assertion c.r.eligible_for_qss
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_people_count = 1
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_single
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_mfj
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_mfs
  assertion not c.r.has_multiple_eligible_filing_statuses
  assertion c.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion not c.r.unsupported
  assertion c.r.recommended_filing_status = QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
  # Known-bad: QSS preempts HoH
  assertion chose_hoh.r.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
  assertion chose_hoh.r.unsupported
  # Known-bad: a surviving spouse is not taxed as single (DF-BUG(20-a))
  assertion chose_single.r.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
  # Without 2(a)(2)(B), not a surviving spouse: head of household instead
  assertion not no_joint.r.eligible_for_qss
  assertion no_joint.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion no_joint.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion no_joint.r.recommended_filing_status = HeadOfHousehold
```

### Divorced, no dependents: single only

IRC 7703(a)(2): "an individual legally separated from his spouse under a
decree of divorce ... shall not be considered as married". With no
qualifying person the filer is neither a head of household nor a surviving
spouse, so single is the only status (Pub. 501 p 6). Known-bad outputs
rejected: HoH, MFS and MFJ are each knocked out.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDivorcedNoDependents:
  c scope Case
  chose_hoh scope Case
  chose_mfs scope Case
  chose_mfj scope Case

scope TestDivorcedNoDependents:
  definition c.marital_status equals Divorced
  definition chose_hoh.marital_status equals Divorced
  definition chose_hoh.filing_status equals HeadOfHousehold
  definition chose_mfs.marital_status equals Divorced
  definition chose_mfs.filing_status equals MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition chose_mfj.marital_status equals Divorced
  definition chose_mfj.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  assertion c.r.eligible_for_single
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_mfj
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_mfs
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_qss
  assertion c.r.eligibility.eligible_filing_status_count = 1
  assertion not c.r.has_multiple_eligible_filing_statuses
  assertion c.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion not c.r.unsupported
  assertion c.r.recommended_filing_status = Single
  # Known-bad: every other status
  assertion chose_hoh.r.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
  assertion chose_mfs.r.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
  assertion chose_mfj.r.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
```

## Further cases

### Unmarried with a qualifying child: head of household, not single (DF-BUG(20-a))

IRC 1(c) taxes as single "every individual (other than a surviving spouse ...
or the head of a household as defined in section 2(b)) who is not a married
individual"; Pub. 501 p 6: "Your filing status is single if you are
considered unmarried and you don't qualify for another filing status." DF
offers single and HoH; here HoH only. Known-bad output rejected: choosing
single is knocked out. Without the upkeep (2(b)(1), "over half of the cost of
maintaining the household") there is no qualifying person and single is the
only status.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestUnmarriedWithChild:
  c scope Case
  chose_single scope Case
  no_upkeep scope Case

scope TestUnmarriedWithChild:
  definition c.has_child equals true
  definition c.filing_status equals HeadOfHousehold
  definition chose_single.has_child equals true
  definition no_upkeep.has_child equals true
  definition no_upkeep.upkeep equals false
  assertion c.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion not c.r.eligible_for_single
  assertion not c.r.has_multiple_eligible_filing_statuses
  assertion c.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion c.r.recommended_filing_status = HeadOfHousehold
  # Known-bad: single for a head of household
  assertion not chose_single.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion chose_single.r.unsupported
  # No upkeep: single only
  assertion not no_upkeep.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion no_upkeep.r.eligible_for_single
  assertion no_upkeep.r.is_filing_status_valid
```

### Married living together: the recommendation follows the chosen separate return

DF `/recommendedFilingStatus`: MFJ unless the filer chose a separate return,
then HoH if eligible, else MFS. A couple living together all year, no
children: MFJ and MFS eligible. The same filer living apart with the son and
choosing MFS is recommended HoH (Pub. 501 p 7: "If you qualify to file as
head of household, instead of as married filing separately, your tax may be
lower").

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRecommendationMarried:
  mfj scope Case
  mfs scope Case
  apart_mfs scope Case

scope TestRecommendationMarried:
  definition mfj.marital_status equals Married
  definition mfj.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfs.marital_status equals Married
  definition mfs.filing_status equals MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition apart_mfs.marital_status equals Married
  definition apart_mfs.lived_together_all_year equals false
  definition apart_mfs.lived_together_months equals LivedApartAllYear
  definition apart_mfs.has_child equals true
  definition apart_mfs.filing_status equals MarriedFilingSeparately
  assertion mfj.r.eligible_for_mfj and mfj.r.eligible_for_mfs
  assertion mfj.r.eligibility.eligible_filing_status_count = 2
  assertion mfj.r.treat_as_mfj
  assertion mfj.r.recommended_filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
  assertion mfs.r.treat_as_mfs
  assertion mfs.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion mfs.r.recommended_filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately
  assertion apart_mfs.r.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion apart_mfs.r.is_filing_status_valid
  assertion apart_mfs.r.recommended_filing_status = HeadOfHousehold
  # Known-bad: MFJ is not recommended to a filer who chose to file separately
  assertion mfs.r.recommended_filing_status != MarriedFilingJointly
```

### The recommendation is always an eligible status

`FilingStatusEligibility` on every combination of its stage-1 and stage-2
inputs that a return can produce (a filer is married, widowed in the tax
year, or neither; MFJ needs "married"; HoH and QSS need their filer-side
answer and a qualifying person; QSS needs "not married"), for each chosen
status: the recommendation is eligible, and the chosen status is valid
exactly when it is not knocked out.

```catala
declaration scope Elig:
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context married content boolean
  context mfj content boolean
  context could_hoh content boolean
  context could_qss content boolean
  context hoh_count content integer
  context qss_count content integer
  output e content S.FilingStatusEligibility
  output recommendation_is_eligible condition

scope Elig:
  definition filing_status equals Single
  definition married equals false
  definition mfj equals false
  definition could_hoh equals false
  definition could_qss equals false
  definition hoh_count equals 0
  definition qss_count equals 0
  definition e equals
    output of S.FilingStatusEligibility with {
      -- filing_status: filing_status
      -- marital_status_allows_filing_married: married
      -- eligible_for_mfj: mfj
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_hoh: could_hoh
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_qss: could_qss
      -- hoh_qualifying_people_count: hoh_count
      -- qss_qualifying_people_count: qss_count }
  rule recommendation_is_eligible under condition
    match e.recommended_filing_status with pattern
    -- Single: e.eligible_for_single
    -- MarriedFilingJointly: mfj
    -- MarriedFilingSeparately: e.eligible_for_mfs
    -- HeadOfHousehold: e.eligible_for_hoh
    -- QualifyingSurvivingSpouse: e.eligible_for_qss
  consequence fulfilled

#[test]
declaration scope TestRecommendationEligible:
  single_none scope Elig
  single_hoh scope Elig
  widow_qss_and_hoh scope Elig
  married_together scope Elig
  married_apart_hoh_chose_mfs scope Elig
  nra_spouse_hoh scope Elig
  nra_spouse_alone scope Elig

scope TestRecommendationEligible:
  definition single_hoh.could_hoh equals true
  definition single_hoh.hoh_count equals 2
  definition widow_qss_and_hoh.could_hoh equals true
  definition widow_qss_and_hoh.could_qss equals true
  definition widow_qss_and_hoh.hoh_count equals 1
  definition widow_qss_and_hoh.qss_count equals 1
  definition widow_qss_and_hoh.filing_status equals QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
  definition married_together.married equals true
  definition married_together.mfj equals true
  definition married_together.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition married_apart_hoh_chose_mfs.married equals true
  definition married_apart_hoh_chose_mfs.mfj equals true
  definition married_apart_hoh_chose_mfs.could_hoh equals true
  definition married_apart_hoh_chose_mfs.hoh_count equals 1
  definition married_apart_hoh_chose_mfs.filing_status equals
    MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition nra_spouse_hoh.married equals true
  definition nra_spouse_hoh.could_hoh equals true
  definition nra_spouse_hoh.hoh_count equals 1
  definition nra_spouse_hoh.filing_status equals HeadOfHousehold
  definition nra_spouse_alone.married equals true
  definition nra_spouse_alone.could_hoh equals true
  definition nra_spouse_alone.filing_status equals MarriedFilingSeparately
  assertion single_none.recommendation_is_eligible
  assertion single_hoh.recommendation_is_eligible
  assertion widow_qss_and_hoh.recommendation_is_eligible
  assertion married_together.recommendation_is_eligible
  assertion married_apart_hoh_chose_mfs.recommendation_is_eligible
  assertion nra_spouse_hoh.recommendation_is_eligible
  assertion nra_spouse_alone.recommendation_is_eligible
  assertion single_none.e.recommended_filing_status = Single
  assertion single_hoh.e.recommended_filing_status = HeadOfHousehold
  assertion widow_qss_and_hoh.e.recommended_filing_status = QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
  assertion not widow_qss_and_hoh.e.eligible_for_hoh
  assertion married_together.e.recommended_filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
  assertion married_apart_hoh_chose_mfs.e.recommended_filing_status = HeadOfHousehold
  assertion nra_spouse_hoh.e.recommended_filing_status = HeadOfHousehold
  assertion nra_spouse_alone.e.recommended_filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately
  # Valid exactly when not knocked out
  assertion single_hoh.e.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
  assertion not single_none.e.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
  assertion not nra_spouse_hoh.e.ko_filing_status_not_eligible
  assertion not widow_qss_and_hoh.e.unsupported
```
